Item # : SCP-5162

Object Class:  Euclid

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5162 is to be kept inside a 6m x 6m chamber with no less than 20.32cm (8 inches) of fireproofing material (asbestos cement, fiberglass, drywall) and 12.7cm (5 inches) thick iron plating upon all surfaces and a blast-proof observation window with emergency blast shielding installed. The opening to the chamber must consist of at least two temperature-controlled and airtight chambers that may be sealed in case of emergency.

Description:  SCP-5162 is an American soldier who fought in World war two, he was a sergeant in the 82nd Airborne Division who fought in Normandy. SCP-5162 has the ability to produce fire and to manipulate it, he also has hysterical strength and can jump approximately 1.5 meters (4.92 ft.) and he doesn't age. SCP-5162 reportedly raided a bunker alone and eliminated 17 Nazi soldiers during the Normandy invasion, 8 bodies were burnt by SCP-5162's fire, 6 were snapped neck, 3 were their bodies were torn apart.

Private █████████ █████████ was SCP-5126's closest friend and was the first one to discover his abilities. After the War he leaves the army, the Foundation tracked SCP-5126's location and was hiding in Siberia.



